This sample is the caller half of a two-agent A2A delegation pattern and cannot
be deployed standalone by the hosted-agents-cloud-e2e workflow, which deploys
each agent folder independently with no cross-agent ordering or wiring.

At startup the caller loads its `a2a-delegation-tools` toolbox (an `a2a_preview`
tool) over MCP. That tool proxies to the sibling `a2a-executor` agent through the
`math-expert-a2a` RemoteA2A connection (target `a2a_executor_endpoint`). When the
caller is deployed on its own, that connection has no live executor A2A endpoint
behind it, so enumerating the delegation tool fails and the MCP session is
terminated — the container crashes before it can serve.

The correct order (deploy `a2a-executor` → it publishes its declarative A2A card
→ deploy `a2a-caller` pointed at the executor's endpoint) is documented in
README.md. The `a2a-executor` half IS exercised by CI on its own. Excluded from
the hosted-agents e2e CI pipeline; see README.md for the manual walkthrough.
